<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Unilateral Declaration of Independence (Rhodesia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1965">1965</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as UDI</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Unilateral Declaration of Independence was issued on 11 November 1965 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ian-smith">Ian Smith</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodesian-front">Rhodesian Front</a> government of Southern Rhodesia, which refused <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s demand for progress to majority rule. Britain and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> declared it illegal and imposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>, and no state recognised Rhodesia. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war that followed ended with the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> in 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/unilateral-declaration-of-independence-rhodesia.jpg" alt="Unilateral Declaration of Independence (Rhodesia)" width="320" height="529" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Rhodesia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unilateral_Declaration_of_Independence_(Rhodesia).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
